From 7391d11181a5a13d567f72236ee2943a72e87eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:50:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] clk: meson: Use the SC2 fixed PLL fractional denominator

SC2 exposes a 19-bit fraction register but its BSP scales positive
fractions by 2^17. The generic default of 2^19 reports the observed
M=166,N=1,OD=1,frac=87381 as 1.994 GHz instead of approximately 2 GHz.
MPLL audio dividers then produce the same +0.3009 percent pitch error
observed independently at the HDMI receiver.

Set the existing frac_max override for this read-only PLL only. Keep
register width, PLL programming, secure CPU clocks and other SoCs intact.
The production arithmetic helper reproduces both rates and retains
integer-fraction behavior. Actual corrected boot and tones remain to test.

Change-Id: I3af3e9b33ce5b799fabca16a1d2189a99a8d41b8
---
 drivers/clk/meson/sc2.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/meson/sc2.c b/drivers/clk/meson/sc2.c
index a1fb78a7ca27..635c0fd03523 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/meson/sc2.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/meson/sc2.c
@@ -165,6 +165,8 @@ static struct clk_regmap sc2_fixed_pll_dco = {
 			.shift   = 0,
 			.width   = 19,
 		},
+		/* SC2's 19-bit field has a 17-bit fractional denominator. */
+		.frac_max = BIT(17),
 		.l = {
 			.reg_off = ANACTRL_FIXPLL_CTRL0,
 			.shift   = 31,
-- 
